.TH ZIP 1 2026-10-19 tugz
.SH NAME
zip \- package files into a zip archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zip
.RI [ \-options ]
.IR archive [ .zip ]
.RI [ path .\|.\|.]
.RB [ \-x
.IR pattern .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zip
adds each
.I path
to
.IR archive ,
creating it if needed, with
.B .zip
appended when the name has no extension.
It is a subset of Info-ZIP Zip 3.0, made for scripts that package
releases, with the same options, messages, and exit statuses.
.PP
An existing archive is merged: matching entries are replaced, new ones
appended, and the rest copied without recompression.
The new archive is written to a temporary file beside the old one and
renamed over it, so an interrupted run leaves the old archive intact.
Zip64 is used as needed.
Names that are UTF-8, and not ASCII, are marked as UTF-8.
.PP
Where entries select files, as under
.B \-u
or
.B \-f
without paths, or with a path not on disk that matches entries, they
select only files within the current directory, never through links,
so refreshing an untrusted archive cannot read other files.
An archive whose entries overlap, as in a zip bomb, is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
Long options may be abbreviated.
Options may be combined
.RB ( \-qr9 ).
.TP
.BR \-0 " .\|.\|. " \-9
Store only, or compress from fastest to best (default 6).
Entries that do not shrink are stored.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recurse\-paths
Recurse into directories.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No messages or warnings.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-strip\-extra
Store no extra attributes (Unix times, owners).
.B \-X\-
negates it.
.TP
.BR \-@ ", " \-\-names\-stdin
Read paths from standard input, one per line.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-junk\-paths
Store names without their directories.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-no\-dir\-entries
Make no entries for directories.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude " \fIpattern\fR .\|.\|."
Leave out paths matching the patterns that follow.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-include " \fIpattern\fR .\|.\|."
Add only paths matching the patterns that follow.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-symlinks
Store symbolic links as links (POSIX).
.TP
.B \-S
Include hidden and system files (Windows).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Replace entries whose files are newer, and add new files.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-freshen
Replace entries whose files are newer, adding none.
.B \-u
and
.B \-f
without paths refresh every entry.
.TP
.BR \-FS ", " \-\-filesync
Replace changed entries and delete those whose files are gone.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delete
Delete the entries that the paths match, as patterns.
.TP
.BR \-nw ", " \-\-no\-wild
Treat
.BR * ,
.BR [ ,
and
.B ]
literally in paths.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Alone, show the version.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-license
Show the license.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-H ", " \-? ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.PP
Other Info-ZIP options are refused (16) rather than ignored, among them
encryption, comments, splits, self-extractor adjustment, line-ending
conversion, streaming, and logging.
.SH REPRODUCIBLE ARCHIVES
Entries within each directory are sorted by name.
With
.BR \-X ,
an archive depends only on the files' contents, names, attributes, and
modification times.
.PP
When
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
is set, to seconds since 1970, times are clamped to it and stored in
UTC, so the archive does not depend on the time zone either.
Without
.BR \-X ,
access times are the epoch itself.
Any integer is accepted, negative too, and times clamp to what entries
can hold: DOS times span 1980 through 2107, and extended timestamps 1901
through 2106.
.BR \-u ,
.BR \-f ,
and
.B \-FS
still compare the files' real times.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR ZIPOPT ", " ZIP
Options applied before the arguments, from
.BR ZIPOPT ,
else
.BR ZIP .
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
See
.BR "REPRODUCIBLE ARCHIVES" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, even when
.B \-u
or
.B \-f
found nothing newer.
.TP
.B 2
The archive ended unexpectedly.
.TP
.B 3
The archive is damaged or unsupported.
.TP
.B 4
Out of memory.
.TP
.B 10
Temporary file failure.
.TP
.B 11
The archive could not be read.
.TP
.B 12
Nothing to do, as when
.B \-i
matches nothing.
.TP
.B 14
Write error.
.TP
.B 15
The archive could not be created or replaced.
.TP
.B 16
Bad or unsupported options.
.TP
.B 18
Some files could not be read, and were left out.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
zip \-qX9r release\-1.2.3.zip build/
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=$(git log \-1 \-\-format=%ct) zip \-qXr src.zip src
zip \-d release.zip \(aq*.o\(aq
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unzip (1),
.BR gzip (1)
